{"name":"Limewash","hex":"#dbd5cb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"limewash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of slaked lime in water, used as a paint or a paintlike coating."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To paint with limewash (slaked lime in water)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limewash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whitewash","blocks":[{"text":"Whitewash, calcimine, kalsomine, calsomine, asbestis or lime paint is a type of paint made from slaked lime (calcium hydroxide, Ca(OH)2) or chalk (calcium carbonate, CaCO3), sometimes known as \"whiting\". Various other additives are sometimes used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Yarloop_wkshop_gnangarra_13.jpg/330px-Yarloop_wkshop_gnangarra_13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitewash","wikidata":"Q378312"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Nicolae_Ionescu_-_The_Whitewashers%2C_1928.jpg/500px-Nicolae_Ionescu_-_The_Whitewashers%2C_1928.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Nicolae_Ionescu_-_The_Whitewashers%2C_1928.jpg/500px-Nicolae_Ionescu_-_The_Whitewashers%2C_1928.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Whitewashers, photographed by Nicolae Ionescu [cs], 1928","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANicolae_Ionescu_-_The_Whitewashers%2C_1928.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Campsite-Oludeniz.JPG/500px-Campsite-Oludeniz.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Campsite-Oludeniz.JPG/1280px-Campsite-Oludeniz.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org